TAM-SESSION-BENCH

Graphical session startup and resource benchmark tool for comparing
Hyprland and tam-pane on Tamlinux.


USAGE

    tam-session-bench startup [--boot 0 | --boots N | --all-boots] [--json]
    tam-session-bench now [--json]
    tam-session-bench sample [--seconds 30 | --minutes M] [--interval 2]
                             [--settle 0] [--label NAME] [--save] [--json]
    tam-session-bench compare [--boots N | --all-boots] [--json]


DESCRIPTION

- startup: Reconstructs per-stage graphical session startup timings
  (UWSM env preload, compositor ready, session target, shell ready, and
  tam-pane internal lua/init/start phases when logged) from the systemd
  user journal.
- now: Live resource snapshot of the active compositor, tamlinux-shell,
  and portals (cgroup memory/peak/swap, PSS/RSS, CPU average, DRM GPU
  VRAM/GTT deduplicated by drm-client-id, plus optional tam-meter power).
- sample: Timed measurement window reporting delta CPU %, delta GPU GFX %,
  context switches/s, PSS/VRAM medians, and optional APU power. Use --save
  to record runs under ~/.local/state/tamlinux/session-bench/ for cross-
  session comparison.
- compare: Side-by-side comparison table across Hyprland and tam-pane from
  journal session history and saved timed samples.

Python 3 stdlib only. No root required.
